diff --git a/content/distributed/REMOTE_GZIPPER_PROTOCOL.md b/content/distributed/REMOTE_GZIPPER_PROTOCOL.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..f9a2e4c7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/content/distributed/REMOTE_GZIPPER_PROTOCOL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# Remote Gzipper protocol, version 1
+
+Version 1 carries only `data_decoder.mojom.Gzipper::Deflate` between the macOS
+Chromium browser process and a Debian worker reachable through Tailscale. It
+carries raw bytes only: Mojo messages and Mojo handles never cross the network.
+
+A connection carries exactly one request and one response, then closes. The
+client allows one outstanding request and uses Chromium asynchronous DNS and
+TCP APIs. This version has no connection reuse or multiplexing.
+
+## Transport requirements
+
+- Bind the worker only to a Tailscale address or another explicitly private
+  interface. Do not expose this protocol publicly.
+- Chromium requires a host-and-port endpoint, an enable switch, and a readable,
+  non-empty token file before it attempts a connection.
+- The token is authentication data, not a loggable diagnostic. Neither browser
+  nor worker may log the token or request/response payload bytes.
+- Separate 10-second connection and request timers cover DNS/connect and
+  write/read work. Timeout, disconnect, authentication, protocol, or worker
+  failures make Chromium use the local Data Decoder for that request.
+
+## Encoding
+
+All integer fields are unsigned and big-endian. `UCD1` is the magic value and
+the protocol version is `1`. Receivers must consume exactly one complete frame;
+bad magic, version, reserved byte, length, or trailing bytes are malformed.
+
+### Request
+
+| Field | Bytes | Value |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| magic | 4 | ASCII `UCD1` |
+| version | 2 | `1` |
+| operation ID | 1 | `1` for `Gzipper::Deflate` |
+| reserved | 1 | `0` |
+| request ID | 8 | Browser-generated nonzero value |
+| authentication length | 4 | Number of authentication-data bytes |
+| payload length | 8 | Number of binary input bytes |
+| authentication data | variable | Required non-empty token bytes |
+| payload | variable | Binary Deflate input |
+
+The fixed request header is 28 bytes. Authentication data is limited to 4 KiB;
+payload data is limited to 64 MiB. Other operation IDs are parsed only so the
+worker can return the explicit `unsupported operation` failure below.
+
+### Response
+
+| Field | Bytes | Value |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| magic | 4 | ASCII `UCD1` |
+| version | 2 | `1` |
+| status | 1 | `1` success or `2` failure |
+| reserved | 1 | `0` |
+| request ID | 8 | The request's ID |
+| error code | 4 | `0` only on success; nonzero on failure |
+| payload length | 8 | Number of binary result bytes |
+| payload | variable | Binary Deflate output or optional failure bytes |
+
+The fixed response header is 28 bytes. A success response has error code `0`.
+A failure response must have a nonzero error code and must not contain partial
+Deflate output.
+
+## Validation and errors
+
+Before Deflate, the worker validates a parsed request in this order:
+
+1. Empty authentication data: error `1` (`missing authentication`).
+2. Missing expected token or unequal token: error `2` (`authentication failed`).
+3. Any operation ID other than `1`: error `3` (`unsupported operation`).
+
+A worker sends a failure response with the same request ID and the corresponding
+error code. Code `4` is malformed frame, `5` is oversized payload, and `6` is
+an internal worker error. Chromium accepts a response only when its request ID
+matches the request; a mismatched, malformed, or otherwise invalid response
+causes local fallback.
+
+## Production worker
+
+The production implementation is the Chromium GN target
+`//content/distributed:distributed_utility_worker`. It is defined only for
+Linux x86_64 and calls Chromium's existing `data_decoder::Gzipper::Deflate`
+implementation. Build it from the same Chromium revision as the macOS browser:
+
+```sh
+gn gen out/distributed-worker --args='target_os="linux" target_cpu="x64"'
+autoninja -C out/distributed-worker distributed_utility_worker
+```
+
+Create a token file readable only by the worker account, then bind the worker
+to the Debian machine's Tailscale address:
+
+```sh
+out/distributed-worker/distributed_utility_worker \
+  --listen-host=100.x.y.z \
+  --listen-port=8765 \
+  --token-file=/run/secrets/distributed-utility-token
+```
+
+The executable rejects wildcard addresses and empty or unreadable token files.
+SIGTERM and SIGINT stop accepting work, disconnect the active request, and exit
+the asynchronous event loop cleanly. It logs startup or configuration errors
+only; authentication data and request/response payloads are never logged.
+
+The repository's `distributed-worker/` Python implementation is a
+non-production development harness for protocol experiments. It is not the
+worker deployed with Chromium.
